      "body": "# Description\n\nFix silently wrong results from Flex Attention `score_mod` with `nvidia-cudnn-frontend` 1.31.0 and newer.\n\nOnly the cuDNN backend implements `score_mod`. The frontend decides whether a graph has a score modifier by reading the record key `fn`, which is the argument name of `sdpa_fp8()`, while `sdpa()` names it `score_mod`. So the frontend does not see the modifier on these graphs. From 1.31.0, its Python engine `sdpa_fwd_prefill_sm100` also accepts 64-dimension heads, so it can serve a Transformer Engine graph as plain attention and drop the modifier without an error.\n\nNVIDIA/cudnn-frontend#1960 fixes the frontend, and the `v1.32.1` tag contains that fix. The `nvidia-cudnn-frontend==1.32.1` wheel on PyPI does not, so `>=1.29.0` still installs the affected code. This PR therefore protects Transformer Engine on all of these versions, without a version pin.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [ ] Documentation change (change only to the documentation, either a fix or a new content)\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\n- [ ] Infra/Build change\n- [ ] Code refactoring\n\n## Changes\n\n- Exclude the Python SDPA engines from Flex Attention `score_mod` graphs, so that the cuDNN backend serves them.\n- Raise an error if a Python engine is still selected, so that a later frontend cannot drop the modifier silently.\n\n## Before and after\n\n`test_dot_product_attention_score_mod` ran on one NVIDIA B200 with each PyPI frontend release.\n\n| Frontend | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1.29.1, 1.30.0 | Backend serves every graph, and the test finds no failures | Same |\n| 1.31.0 | The Python engine serves the `softcap` and `post_scale_bias` graphs. Output differs from the reference: up to 38.8% of elements are outside tolerance | Backend serves every graph, and the test finds no failures |\n| 1.32.0, 1.32.1 | The same engine is selected. SBHD output differs from the reference, and BSHD raises `ValueError: cudnn.sdpa: q: this plan was built for 4 heads of dim 64; got (2, 16, 4, 64)` | Backend serves every graph, and the test finds no failures |\n\n## Validation\n\n`test_dot_product_attention_score_mod` is the regression test: it fails on the affected frontends without this change. The plan names on the run above confirm that backend engines (for example `eng7_k24=2_...`) do not match the excluded `sdpa_fwd` and `sdpa_bwd` names.\n\nThe L0 PyTorch commands ran against an untouched tree of `b0219803` on B200, with CUDA 13.2, PyTorch 2.15.0+cu132, and frontend 1.32.1. No test failed only with this change. That run also included #3795 and #3797.\n\nJAX is not changed. It builds the same kind of graph, but in a JAX-only environment with frontend 1.32.1 the graph at this shape was served by the backend, with or without the exclusion. A JAX environment that also has PyTorch installed was not tested. A100, H100, and SM120 were not tested. #3693 rewrites this path, so this check needs to move if that PR lands first.\n\n# Checklist:\n\n- [x] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\n- [x] The functionality is complete\n- [x] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\n- [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings\n- [ ] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works\n- [ ] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\n",
